.TH HOMELAB-SSO-UI 8 "2026-07-31" "homelab-sso-ui" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
homelab-sso-ui \- Homelab SSO login service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homelab-sso-ui
.br
(started via
.B hypnotoad
under the
.B homelab-sso-ui.service
systemd unit; not normally invoked directly)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B homelab-sso-ui
implements a small OAuth2 authorization-code flow
.RI ( /oauth/authorize ", " /oauth/token ", " /oauth/userinfo )
plus a single-logout endpoint
.RI ( /logout )
as a thin wrapper around
.BR homelab-api (8) 's
existing login and JWT machinery. The OAuth "access_token" issued to
clients
.B is
the homelab-api JWT itself \- this service does not mint a separate
token. It does cache the JWT and refresh token in its own signed IdP
session cookie (see SS session in CONFIGURATION) so a user who already
authenticated once can skip the login form on subsequent requests \-
including for a
.B different
consuming app than the one just used, which is what makes this real
cross-app single sign-on \- and mints a short-lived (60 second), one-time
authorization code per request, held in memory.
.P
Consumers (Roundcube and
.BR homelab-drive-web-ui )
delegate their login
.B and logout
screens to this service instead of checking credentials or managing
sessions themselves. Roundcube in particular has native OAuth2 login
support that works against this service with no custom plugin.
.B /logout
clears the IdP session (so both consumers' auto-redirect-on-unauthenticated
behavior doesn't silently log the user right back in) and redirects to a
caller-supplied
.I redirect_uri
\- restricted to origins matching a registered client's own
.B redirect_uri
to prevent it being used as an open redirect.
.P
It runs as a Mojolicious application under Hypnotoad and is managed via
systemd; it is not intended to be run interactively.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/homelab/sso-ui/config.yml
Main configuration file (YAML). See CONFIGURATION below.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOMELAB_SSO_UI_CONFIG
Overrides the path to the configuration file (default
.IR /etc/homelab/sso-ui/config.yml ).
Set by the shipped systemd unit.
.TP
.B HOMELAB_SSO_UI_HOME
Overrides the base directory used to locate templates
.RI ( templates/ )
and static assets
.RI ( public/ ).
Default:
.IR /usr/share/homelab-sso-ui .
Set by the shipped systemd unit; useful for running from a source
checkout during development.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS homelab_api
.TP
.B base_url
Base URL of the
.B homelab-api
instance this service authenticates users against and validates tokens
through. No default \- required.
.SS secrets
An array of one or more session-signing secrets, for the IdP session
cookie (see SS session below). If you run more than one instance behind a
load balancer, all instances
.B must
use the identical
.B secrets
value, or sessions created by one instance are rejected by another.
Required \- the service refuses to start without it.
.SS session
.TP
.B secure
Boolean (0/1). Marks the IdP session cookie
.BR Secure ;
set to
.I 0
only for local HTTP development. Default:
.IR 1 .
.TP
.B expiry
IdP session lifetime, in seconds. Default:
.I 2592000
(30 days) \- matches
.BR homelab-api 's
refresh-token lifetime, since that's the practical ceiling on how long a
session can keep silently renewing itself anyway. While this session is
valid, a request to
.I /oauth/authorize
for
.B any
registered client skips the login form entirely and redirects straight
back with a fresh authorization code \- this is what makes repeat/
cross-app logins invisible instead of showing a form every time.
.TP
.B cookie_domain
Optional. Scopes a separate, unsigned "session epoch" marker cookie
.RI ( homelab-sso-epoch )
to this domain (e.g.
.IR mailmasker.org )
instead of just this host, so every consuming app under it sees a logout
happen on their very next request \- this is what makes logging out of
one app immediately kill every other app's session too, not just this
service's own. Only meaningful when every consuming app actually lives
under the same parent domain. Unset by default (the marker cookie is then
host-only, same as before this feature existed); consuming apps that
never see a matching cookie simply never trip the check.
.SS clients
A list of OAuth2 clients permitted to use this SSO service. Each entry
has:
.TP
.B client_id
Identifier the client sends in
.I /oauth/authorize
and
.IR /oauth/token .
.TP
.B client_secret
Shared secret the client must present at
.I /oauth/token
to exchange an authorization code for a token. No default \- required
per client; use a long random value.
.TP
.B redirect_uri
The exact URI this service will redirect back to after a successful
login for this client. Requests naming a
.B client_id
whose registered
.B redirect_uri
does not match exactly are rejected before any login form is shown.
.SS server
Hypnotoad listen/worker configuration.
.TP
.B listen
Full listen URL, e.g.
.IR http://0.0.0.0:2502 .
Default:
.IR http://127.0.0.1:2502 .
Deliberately different from
.BR homelab-api 's
default
.RI ( 3000 )
and
.BR homelab-drive-web-ui 's
default
.RI ( 2501 ),
so all three can coexist on one host (e.g. for local/dev testing)
without a port collision.
.TP
.B workers
Number of Hypnotoad worker processes. Default:
.IR 1 .
.B Must stay at 1
unless the in-memory one-time authorization code store is replaced with
a shared backing store \- a code minted by one worker process is not
visible to another.
.TP
.B pid_file
Path to the Hypnotoad PID file. Default:
.IR /var/lib/homelab/sso-ui-hypnotoad.pid .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR homelab-api (8)
.P
Full example configuration:
.I /usr/share/homelab-sso-ui/config/sso-ui.example.yml
